# Accurate Medical Center — UI/UX Redesign Plan

I have completed a thorough audit of the repository (`src/app`, `src/components`, `src/config`, `globals.css`) and drafted a comprehensive UI redesign plan centered around AMC's brand (Lemon/Black/Grey) and patient-focused vision. 

The complete detailed plan has been saved to the repository at [docs/AMC-UI-REDESIGN-PLAN.md](file:///c:/Users/USER/Accurate%20Medical%20Center/docs/AMC-UI-REDESIGN-PLAN.md).

## Key Audit Findings

> [!WARNING]
> **Blockers Found:**
> - `DashboardLayout` has the user role hardcoded as `DOCTOR`. It needs to read the actual session.
> - The `billing` module is currently using USD (`$`) instead of NGN (`₦`).
> - The dashboards are currently displaying hardcoded fake patient data (e.g., "John Doe") instead of real data from the backend.
> - The topbar has cosmetic search and fake notifications/user profiles.

> [!NOTE]
> **Design Deficiencies:**
> - The UI feels like a generic SaaS template, lacking the premium hospital identity.
> - Missing a robust library of UI components (currently only 5 exist: Button, Card, Input, Logo, Table).
> - Missing consistent loading (Skeleton) and empty states.

> [!TIP]
> **What We Will Keep:**
> - The `globals.css` color token system is a strong foundation (we will expand it).
> - The `nav.ts` navigation configuration is comprehensive and correct.
> - Existing API integrations (like the one in `reception/patients`) will be preserved.

## Proposed Architecture & Design System

We will build a professional, patient-centric interface that communicates Trust, Precision, and Modern Healthcare.

### 1. Global Application Shell
- **Sidebar:** Role-aware, grouped sections, collapsible, with a real user profile at the bottom.
- **Topbar:** Real session context, breadcrumbs, and a CMD+K global search palette.
- **Mobile:** The sidebar will transition into a touch-friendly drawer, supplemented by a bottom navigation bar for core tasks.

### 2. Role-Specific Dashboards
Instead of generic stat cards, dashboards will be operational workspaces:
- **Reception:** Live waiting queues, quick patient registration.
- **Doctor:** Clinical queue, patient summaries, and prioritized action items (abnormal labs).
- **Billing:** Revenue in NGN (`₦`), active invoice queue.

### 3. Patient Experience
The patient profile will be a clinical workspace featuring a unified Patient Header (photo, allergies, alerts) and a comprehensive medical timeline.

## Implementation Sequence (The First 5 Phases)

We will execute this incrementally to ensure we don't break existing functionality.

### Phase 1: Design System Foundation
- Expand `globals.css` with semantic tokens.
- Build missing core components: `Badge`, `StatusBadge`, `Skeleton`, `EmptyState`, `Avatar`, `Toast`.
- Enhance existing components: `Button` (loading state), `Input` (icons, errors).

### Phase 2: Application Shell
- Update `DashboardLayout` to use the real session.
- Rebuild the `Sidebar` (collapse, mobile drawer) and `Topbar` (breadcrumbs, user info).

### Phase 3: Authentication Redesign
- Redesign the `login` page to use the real AMC logo and proper hospital branding.

### Phase 4: Operational Dashboards
- Implement role-specific dashboards (Reception, Doctor, Billing) with real data and functional queues. Fix the currency to NGN.

### Phase 5: Patient Management
- Redesign the patient directory.
- Build the comprehensive Patient Profile workspace.

*(See the full 24-phase roadmap in the `docs` folder for details on all departments including Lab, Pharmacy, Radiology, etc.)*

